#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/ev-charging-control/surplus-charging.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/home-assistant.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Settings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "OpenEMS: Grid-optimized charge"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
msgid ""
"Grid-optimized charge decides **when and how strongly the storage is charged "
"with solar power**. It has two goals:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
msgid ""
"**Complying with the feed-in limit:** Many systems may only feed part of "
"their power into the grid (e.g. 60 % or 70 %). Whatever exceeds this at "
"midday is charged into the storage instead of being curtailed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
msgid ""
"**Not filling the storage too early:** If the storage is already full in the "
"morning, there is no room left for the midday peak, and solar power is lost. "
"Charging is therefore distributed over the day. The storage should only be "
"full towards the end of the surplus period."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
msgid ""
"In OpenEMS, this function is called **Controller.Ess.GridOptimizedCharge** "
"(usually with the ID `+ctrlGridOptimizedCharge0+`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "What this looks like over the day"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-this-looks-like-over-the-day
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
msgid ""
"In the **early morning** there is no significant surplus yet, and the "
"function waits."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-this-looks-like-over-the-day
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
msgid ""
"In the **morning** the storage charges at a reduced rate. The rest of the "
"surplus is fed in, as far as the feed-in limit allows."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-this-looks-like-over-the-day
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
msgid ""
"At **midday** the feed-in would exceed the limit. Now the storage charges at "
"least enough for the limit to be complied with."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-this-looks-like-over-the-day
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
msgid "In the **afternoon**, up to the target time, the storage becomes full."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-this-looks-like-over-the-day
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
msgid "If the two goals conflict, the **feed-in limit takes priority**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "The target time"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-the-target-time
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
msgid "What matters is when the storage should be full:"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-the-target-time
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
msgid ""
"**Automatic** (default): OpenEMS looks at the xref:user/schedule/"
"forecasts.adoc[forecast] and searches for the time from which solar "
"production is expected to no longer exceed consumption. A safety buffer is "
"subtracted from this time."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-the-target-time
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
msgid "**Manual:** You specify a fixed time, e.g. 17:00."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-the-target-time
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
msgid ""
"**Off:** The storage does not delay charging. The feed-in limit is still "
"complied with."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-the-target-time
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
msgid "The safety buffer is determined by the **risk propensity**:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Setting\n"
"| Buffer\n"
"| Effect\n"
"\n"
"| Low\n"
"| 3 hours\n"
"| The storage almost certainly becomes full, but slightly less room remains at midday.\n"
"| Medium (default)\n"
"| 2 hours\n"
"| balanced\n"
"| High\n"
"| 1 hour\n"
"| More room for midday peaks; on overcast days the storage may not become completely full.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "When the function does not intervene"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-when-the-function-does-not-intervene
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
msgid "If the storage cannot be controlled."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-when-the-function-does-not-intervene
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
msgid "In island mode (emergency power)."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-when-the-function-does-not-intervene
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
msgid "As long as there has been no clear solar surplus yet on that day."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-when-the-function-does-not-intervene
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
msgid ""
"If the permitted feed-in is very small. Meaningful control is then not "
"possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-when-the-function-does-not-intervene
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
msgid ""
"What the function is currently doing is shown by the states “Charging "
"delayed” and “Feed-in limitation”, e.g. “Charge limit active”, “no remaining "
"time” or “End time not calculated”."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Together with a time-of-use tariff"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-together-with-a-time-of-use-tariff
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
msgid ""
"If price control for a xref:user/storage-control/time-of-use-"
"tariffs.adoc[time-of-use tariff] is also active, grid-optimized charge **no "
"longer works independently**. Otherwise, two functions would be adjusting "
"the storage at the same time. Instead, the price control optimizer plans "
"both together:"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-together-with-a-time-of-use-tariff
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
msgid "It can then also charge the storage in a “delayed” or “limited” manner."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-together-with-a-time-of-use-tariff
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
msgid ""
"The settings of grid-optimized charge remain effective: the risk propensity "
"(as a reserve for the state of charge) or the fixed target time."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-together-with-a-time-of-use-tariff
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
msgid ""
"If price control is switched off, grid-optimized charge takes over again by "
"itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-together-with-a-time-of-use-tariff
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
msgid ""
"The result can be seen in the xref:user/schedule/overview.adoc[schedule]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/grid-optimized-charge.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Setting\n"
"| Default\n"
"| Meaning\n"
"\n"
"| Mode\n"
"| Automatic\n"
"| Automatic / Manual / Off\n"
"| Risk propensity\n"
"| Medium\n"
"| see above\n"
"| Target time\n"
"| 17:00\n"
"| only in Manual mode\n"
"| Feed-in limit\n"
"| –\n"
"| is set centrally in the system settings (Meta), no longer in this function\n"
msgstr ""
